# Code owners for Dsinha97/deepayan-sinha-portfolio — mirrors fpl-app.
#
# On its own this changes nothing: ownership is enforced only once "Require
# review from Code Owners" is on in the `main` ruleset, and that rule is
# deliberately off. GitHub does not let a pull request author approve their own
# pull request, so on a one-person repo a Code-Owner review requirement, paired
# with the ruleset's no-bypass rule, would block every merge including the
# owner's. Enable it when a second maintainer exists — that is the trigger, not
# a date.
#
# What it does today: make ownership explicit, and auto-request review from the
# owner on any pull request, including one from an outside contributor's fork.

